GPS of the SM-T560 (Broadcom BCM47520, hosted, UART3)
====================================================

The receiver needs Broadcom's proprietary glgps engine from the stock
firmware (KTU84P.T560XXU0APL1, Android 4.4). The files are never part of
the public tree. Release builds carry them in the vendor image
(device.mk, from proprietary/gps on the build host):

  /vendor/lib/gpsblobs/gps.default.so       stock /system/lib/hw/gps.default.so
  /vendor/lib/gpsblobs/gpsd                 stock /system/bin/gpsd
  /vendor/lib/gpsblobs/libsprd_agps_agent.so  stock /system/lib/
  /vendor/lib/gpsblobs/gps.xml              stock /system/etc/gps.xml, edited

The legacy HAL is loaded from there. gpsd needs libssl, libcrypto and
libstdc++ of /system, so init copies it with libsprd_agps_agent.so,
libgpsd_shim.so (this tree) and gps.xml to /data/vendor/gps/blobs on every
boot and runs it from there (init.gtelwifi.rc).

Changes to the blobs, DT_NEEDED only (patchelf):
- gpsd: libgui.so -> libgpsd_shim.so, drop libstlport.so and libicuuc.so,
  RUNPATH $ORIGIN (for libsprd_agps_agent.so and the shim)
- gps.default.so: libstlport.so -> libgpsd_shim.so

- gps.default.so: libstdc++.so -> libc++.so (operator new/delete and the
  __cxa guards; there is no libstdc++ in the vendor namespace)

gps.xml: PortName /dev/ttyS3, GpioNStdbyPath
/sys/devices/platform/gps-power/state, LbsEnable and HttpSyncLto false
(the Broadcom LTO server is gone, so cold starts take minutes).
NvStorageDir, LtoDir and LogDirectory stay /data/system/gps/: glgps creates
its server pipe (.gps.interface.pipe.to_gpsd) in NvStorageDir, and the HAL
looks for it in /data/system/gps/ (hardcoded).

Tested 05.11.2026: chip ID $PGLOR,0,RID,47520, UART3 without errors,
~32 mA while tracking, NMEA through glgps -> HAL -> bridge -> GPSTest.

init bind-mounts the blob directory on /vendor/lib/gpsblobs, where
android.hardware.gnss-service.gtelwifi loads gps.default.so from (vendor
linker namespace), and starts glgps (vendor.gpsd) when gpsd is present.
Kernel side: UART3, LDO_CAMD, LDO_SDIO and GPS_PWR_EN (patch 0101).
